{"entries":[{"caption":"Directed acyclic graph representing the hypothesized causal relationships among day of year, nightly temperature, relative humidity, lunar phase, and bat acoustic activity. Arrows indicate the assumed direction of causal influence. Day of year represents seasonal structure in bat activity and environmental conditions not otherwise represented by the measured nightly covariates. Temperature was assumed to influence relative humidity in addition to having a direct effect on bat activity. Relative humidity and lunar phase were also hypothesized to directly influence bat activity. The graph was used to guide model specification and interpretation of total seasonal and conditional environmental associations.","key":"fig-dag","order":{"number":1,"section":[1,3,0,0,0,0,0]}}],"headings":["methods","study-area-and-acoustic-surveys","acoustic-classification-and-activity-index","causal-structure-and-seasonal-activity","characteristic-echolocation-frequency-groups","bayesian-generalized-additive-models","priors-computation-and-model-assessment"]}